LodeMiner is free to download and use. It is not open source. By installing or running it you agree
to these terms.

1. What you may do
   - Run LodeMiner on any number of your own computers, for personal or commercial mining.
   - Share the official, unmodified download (the release zip or a link to the release page) with
     others, as long as you do not charge for it and keep every file in it unchanged.

2. What you may not do
   - Sell LodeMiner, rent it out, or bundle it with something you sell.
   - Modify the program, or remove, change or bypass the developer fee or any notice in it.
   - Reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble it, except where the law allows this regardless of
     this license.
   - Publish modified copies or present it as your own work.

3. Developer fee
   LodeMiner mines for its developer for 1 % of the time your GPUs mine for you, kept as a running
   balance and paid in short slices: 30 seconds after about 5 minutes of mining (paid in advance),
   then about 60 seconds for every 100 minutes you mine. Time while mining is paused, the GPUs are
   too hot or no pool is connected does not count. The slices run on the pool you are connected to
   or, if that pool does not take the developer login (it refuses or does not answer the login, or
   drops the connection right after it) or keeps rejecting the developer's shares, on Kryptex's
   pool qtc-eu.kryptex.network:7049. The fee is shown in the miner's log every time it runs. It is
   how the project is paid for.

4. Open-source parts
   LodeMiner is built on Quantus Network's quantus-miner, which is licensed under the Apache License
   2.0 (see LICENSE-APACHE-2.0 and NOTICE), and on open-source libraries listed in
   THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt. Those parts stay under their own licenses; nothing here limits the rights
   those licenses give you for them.

5. No warranty
   LodeMiner is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. Mining puts sustained load on your
   graphics card, power supply and cooling, and uses electricity. You run it at your own risk and are
   responsible for your hardware, your power bill, the pools you connect to and the laws where you
   live.

6. Limitation of liability
   To the extent the law allows, the author is not liable for any damage or loss from using or not
   being able to use LodeMiner, including hardware damage, lost earnings or lost data.

7. Termination
   If you break these terms, your right to use LodeMiner ends. Sections 4 to 6 still apply.

8. Changes
   New versions may come with new terms. The terms shipped with a version apply to that version.

